          "topic": "Trigonometry",
          "question": "If sin θ = 3/5, find cos θ (θ is acute)",
          "options": ["3/4", "4/5", "5/4", "4/3"],
          "correctAnswer": 1,
          "explanation": "Using Pythagoras: cos² θ = 1 - sin² θ = 1 - 9/25 = 16/25, so cos θ = 4/5",
          "workingSteps": [
            "Step 1: sin² θ + cos² θ = 1",
            "Step 2: cos² θ = 1 - sin² θ",
            "Step 3: cos² θ = 1 - (3/5)² = 1 - 9/25 = 16/25",
            "Step 4: cos θ = √(16/25) = 4/5 (positive since θ is acute)"
          ]
        },
